      "comments": [
        {
          "type": "improvement",
          "priority": "low",
          "timestamp": "2026-05-31T17:20:49Z",
          "note": "work-package.js: The dialogue button click handler stores `data-repo` and `data-slug` as separate HTML attributes on each button element. Consider whether storing them as a composite `data-ns` (e.g. `repo/slug`) would simplify the HTML, though the current approach is consistent with the rest of the codebase's separate-param convention."
        },
        {
          "type": "debt",
          "priority": "low",
          "timestamp": "2026-05-31T17:20:49Z",
          "note": "run-log.js: The `fetchAndAppend` and initial `API.getRunLogEntries` calls are inside closures that close over `repo` and `slug` from the outer function scope. This is correct but could be made more explicit by passing them as parameters if the function is ever extracted — low priority but worth noting if refactoring is planned."
        },
        {
          "type": "debt",
          "priority": "medium",
          "timestamp": "2026-05-31T17:20:49Z",
          "note": "orchestrator-widgets.js (line 278): `API.getRunLogEntries(slug, filename, afterLine)` still uses the old bare-slug 3-arg form and is NOT covered by this WP. This will produce a broken API call at runtime until that file is also migrated. It appears to be a known unmigrated caller — verify it is covered by another WP in this plan."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "qa",
      "status": "PASS",
      "started_at": "2026-05-31T17:21:55Z",
      "completed_at": "2026-05-31T17:23:24Z",
      "duration_ms": 89000,
      "summary": [
        "Verified implementation of diagnostic logging in resolveProjectStore() catch block (api.ts lines 204–212). Change confirmed via git diff: bare `catch {}` upgraded to `catch (err)` with `process.stderr.write(...)` emitting slug, optional repo, and error message.",
        "AC1 PASS: second catch block logs to stderr via process.stderr.write.",
        "AC2 PASS: log message includes slug=\\\"...\\\", optional repo=\\\"...\\\", and the error message string — sufficient operator context.",
        "AC3 PASS: notFound() still called after logging; function return type and external error-handling behaviour unchanged (additive logging only).",
        "Full regression suite: 2829/2829 tests pass across 92 test files — no regressions."
      ],
      "metrics": {
        "test_coverage": "92 test files",
        "tests_passed": 2829,
        "tests_failed": 0
      },
      "comments": [
        {
          "type": "improvement",
          "priority": "low",
          "timestamp": "2026-05-31T17:23:24Z",
          "note": "The first catch block (resolveProjectDir failure, lines 190–197) intentionally has no stderr logging — the NOT_FOUND/AMBIGUOUS downgrade is a security decision (prevents cross-namespace existence leak). This is correct per the existing inline comment and is out of scope for this WP."
        },
        {
          "type": "improvement",
          "priority": "low",
          "timestamp": "2026-05-31T17:23:24Z",
          "note": "No dedicated unit test for the new stderr log line exists; the change is low-risk (additive) and the existing api.ts test coverage exercises the function indirectly. A targeted unit test mocking process.stderr.write would be a nice-to-have for future hardening."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "status_changed_at": "2026-05-31T17:13:06Z",
  "last_updated": "2026-05-31T17:23:24Z",
  "handoff_notes": [
    {
      "from_agent": "Developer",
      "to_agent": "QA",
      "timestamp": "2026-05-31T17:20:49Z",
      "notes": [
        "work-package.js: `renderWorkPackageDetail(app, repo, slug, wpId)` — all API calls updated to namespaced `(repo, slug)` form; dialogue buttons carry `data-repo` attribute for content fetching.",
        "run-log.js: `renderRunLog(app, repo, slug, filename)` — both `getRunLogEntries` calls (initial + incremental poll) pass `(repo, slug, filename, afterLine)`.",
        "Tests updated: run-log.test.ts and dialogue-qa.test.ts fully migrated to new signatures. 2829/2829 tests pass.",
        "Remaining view migration: project-detail.js (`renderProjectDetail`, `renderPlan`, `renderSynthesis`) still uses bare-slug form — that is a separate WP."
      ]
    },
    {
      "from_agent": "QA",
      "to_agent": "Reviewer",
      "timestamp": "2026-05-31T17:23:24Z",
      "notes": [
        "api.ts resolveProjectStore() second catch block: stderr logging confirmed correct and additive. All 3 AC met. 2829/2829 tests pass. Ready for code review."
      ]
    }
  ]
}

